<DocsLayout
  title="Feature generators"
  subtitle="Involute gears, ISO metric threads, helices and sheet-metal strips with flat patterns: exact profiles and meshes from a few numbers."
  description="CADCAMFUN feature generators: gear dimensions and involute outlines, ISO thread sizes and helical thread solids, coil helices, sheet-metal outlines and developed length, with real outputs and 3D examples."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="purpose" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Feature generators</h2>
    <p>Feature generators turn a few engineering numbers into exact profiles or meshes: an involute gear from module and tooth count, an ISO thread from diameter and pitch, a helix from radius and pitch, a bent strip from a centre line and a thickness. Each is a pure function in <code>packages/core/src/cad</code>; the editor, the assistant and the CAM model call the same function, so all three see the same part.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Generator</th><th>File</th><th>Main exports</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Involute spur gear</td><td><code>gear.ts</code></td><td>gearDimensions, gearOutline, MIN_GEAR_TEETH = 6</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ISO metric thread</td><td><code>thread.ts</code> (124 lines)</td><td>threadSizes, threadProblem, threadTool, threadGroove</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Helix / coil</td><td><code>helix.ts</code> (41 lines)</td><td>coilGeometry, stepsPerTurn, COIL_STEPS_PER_TURN = 32, COIL_MAX_TURNS = 60</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sheet metal</td><td><code>sheet-metal.ts</code> (235 lines)</td><td>sheetOutline, developedLength, withHems, flatPatternDrawing, flatPatternDxf</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="gear" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Involute gears</h2>
    <p>Pitch radius m·z/2, tip radius pitch + m, root radius pitch − 1.25·m, flanks the involute of the base circle r_p·cos α (ISO 53 / DIN 867). The outline is one counter-clockwise ring about the origin with tooth 0 centred on +X. When the teeth would come to a point before the tip circle (few teeth, a large pressure angle), the tip is pulled in by bisection to where the tooth is still 2 % of a pitch wide.</p>
