  <section id="thread" class="doc-section">
    <h2>ISO metric threads</h2>
    <p>A modelled thread is real helical geometry: a core cylinder at the root united with a ridge swept along a helix with the profile kept radial, clipped to the thread length. External threads have their core at d₃ = d − 1.22687·P and a ridge up to d; internal ones are the tool that cuts a tapped hole, core at D₁ = D − 1.08253·P (the tap drill) and a groove out to D. The flank is cut square to the helix and the axial widths are corrected by the cosine of the helix angle so pitch and crest widths are exact.</p>
