  <section id="sheet" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Sheet metal</h2>
    <p>A sheet-metal profile is a centre line thickened to a strip of constant thickness, with the material on the left, right or both sides, and inside bend radius r on every corner. <code>developedLength</code> unbends it with a K-factor (default 0.44): each bend contributes (r + K·t)·θ and each straight run loses the setback of its neighbouring bends.</p>
